# Agent credentials for the Hermes instance — provider API keys and anything
# else the agent itself reads from the environment.
# Copy to agent.env and fill in:  cp agent.env.example agent.env
#
# The compose file loads this with `env_file:`, so every uncommented line here
# becomes an environment variable inside the container. Hermes deliberately
# does not scrub credential env vars at startup (hermes_cli/env_loader.py:
# shell exports are a documented way to supply them), so keys set here are
# picked up by the gateway and the dashboard alike.
#
# Precedence: a key written into data/.env — which is what the dashboard's
# settings page edits, and what `hermes setup` writes — WINS over the value
# here. That is `get_env_value_prefer_dotenv`, and it exists so rotating a key
# in .env mid-session is not shadowed by a stale inherited value. So treat this
# file as the seed, and expect the dashboard to take over once you use it.
#
# This file is gitignored. Never commit real keys.
#
# NOTE: no quotes and no `export`. Compose's env_file parser is not a shell —
# it keeps quotes as part of the value, so OPENROUTER_API_KEY="sk-..." sends
# the quotes to the API and produces a confusing 401.
#
# A blank value is treated as unset: every consumer goes through
# `has_usable_secret`, which rejects anything under 4 characters, so leaving
# the placeholder below empty is harmless.

# --- OpenRouter — https://openrouter.ai/keys -------------------------------
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Anthropic — https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys ---------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- OpenAI — https://platform.openai.com/api-keys -------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Google AI Studio / Gemini — https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey ----
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Others the upstream .env.example documents ----------------------------
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY=
# NOVITA_API_KEY=
# GLM_API_KEY=
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=
#
# The full list, with base-URL overrides and the non-LLM integrations
# (search, messaging, TTS), is in the source tree's own .env.example:
#   $HERMES_SOURCE_DIR/.env.example
